            <ArticleTitle>Antinociceptive activity of Polygonum hydropiper.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>704-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The hexane, ethylacetate and methanol extracts of Polygonum hydropiper whole plant administered to mice at doses of 250 and 500 mg/kg, showed a significant activity on acetic acid-induced writhing. Within the tested extracts, the ethylacetate one showed the most significant activity.</AbstractText>
